STL is made up of 3 things:
[1] Containers  : The actual data structure that owns the data. This is what you would think of typically when you think of Collections in other languages
[2] Algorithms  : They are blind of the containers. They take in iterators, typically begin and end and operate upon them
[3] Iterators   : Different iterators will invoke different methods on the containers 

